    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "\nThis three bedroom bungalow is excellently located close to Murrisk village with lovely views of Croagh Patrick.\n\nThe house was built circa 1986. Its floor area measures approximately 81.1 sq m / 873 sq ft. Accommodation comprises of entrance porch, entrance hall, living room, dining room, kitchenette, three bedrooms and a bathroom. \nThe property is heated by an excellent Grant Vortex condensing boiler, with additional heating provided by a stove with a back boiler.\n\nExternally, the house sits on a site measuring approximately 0.12 ha/0.3 acres which gives a potential purchaser the option to extend subject to planning permission.\n\nMurrisk is situated at the foot of Croagh Patrick, an attractive coastal village located between Westport and Louisburgh towns. The village's amenities include Murrisk National School and two restaurant/bars. A pebble beach and Murrisk Pier is located 250 metres from the property. A number of excellent sandy beaches are within a short drive and Westport town is a ten minute drive.\n\nASKING PRICE: 379,000"
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "\nEntrance Porch - 1.5m x 1.0\n\n\nEntrance Hall - 3.2m x 1.6m & 4.09m x 1.03m\nSolid ash floor, built in storage\n\nLiving Room - 4.97m x 3.35m\nDual aspect windows with Croagh Patrick views, solid ash floor, open fireplace, curtains\n\nKitchenette - 2.88m x 2.24m\nFully tiled, built in units\n\nDining Room - 4.1m x 3.53m\nHotpress, tiled floor, solid fuel stove with back boiler\n\nBedroom One - 4.8m x 3.34m\nCarpeted, built in wardrobe, curtains\n\nBedroom Two - 3.5m x 2.7m\nCarpeted, blinds\n\nBedroom Three - 2.72m x 2.38m\nCarpeted, curtains, blinds\n\nBathroom - 2.48m x 2.0\nFully tiled, bath/electric shower, wc, whb\n\n"
      },
